spi: spidev: add the missing "spidev" spi_device_id for "qti,spidev"

0402-spi-spidev-add-compatible-string-qti-spidev.patch added the OF compatible
"qti,spidev" to spidev_dt_ids[] but not the matching entry in
spidev_spi_ids[].  __spi_register_driver() uses "spi:" modaliases (not "of:")
for module autoloading, so it walks its own of_match_table and warns for every
compatible that has no spi_device_id (vendor prefix stripped):

  SPI driver spidev has no spi_device_id for qti,spidev

Add the ID, following the existing pattern of "silabs,em3581" -> "em3581" and
"siliconlabs,si3210" -> "si3210".  This only silences that boot warning and
restores a consistent "spi:spidev" modalias; binding still happens exclusively
through the OF compatible and spidev_of_check() still rejects a bare "spidev"
node in DT.

--- a/drivers/spi/spidev.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spidev.c
@@ -716,6 +716,7 @@
 	{ .name = "spi-authenta" },
 	{ .name = "em3581" },
 	{ .name = "si3210" },
+	{ .name = "spidev" },
 	{},
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(spi, spidev_spi_ids);
